{{/*
The Workspace-scoped client (ADR 0017, "Form B"). For every entity that carries the
workspace mixin it generates distinct wrapper types behind `client.Scoped(ws)`:
creates cannot name a Workspace, every reference id set on a create/update is verified
against the same Workspace when the builder is saved, and reads, update-by-id and
delete-by-id are confined to the Workspace. A wrapper keeps its write as a recipe (its
predicates and what its setters set) and builds the ent builder only when the write runs,
on the client of the scope it runs on: the scope's own, or the transaction that carries
its Audit entries (write<N>), so that client's hooks apply from the start. Regenerate
with `mise run generate`.
*/}}
{{ define "scoped" }}
{{ template "header" $ }}

